narrative:
## What Are Strings?

A **string** is just a piece of text. In XIOM, strings are written between double quotes, like `"hello"` or `"My name is Alex"`. You've been using strings since your very first program — every time you wrote `io.println("...")`, you were using a string!

Strings aren't just for printing — you can do lots of things with them.

### Gluing Strings Together

You can stick two strings together with the `+` sign. This is called **concatenation** (con-CAT-uh-nation). It's like gluing two pieces of paper to make one longer piece:

```xiom
fn main() {
  let greeting = "Hello, " + "world!";
  io.println(greeting);  // Prints: Hello, world!
}
```

You can also glue a string variable with another string:

```xiom
fn main() {
  let first = "Alex";
  let last = "Chen";
  let full = first + " " + last;  // The middle " " adds a space
  io.println(full);  // Prints: Alex Chen
}
```

### Counting Letters with `string.str_len()`

Want to know how long a string is? XIOM has a built-in tool called `string.str_len()` that counts the characters. It's like putting a ruler next to your text:

```xiom
fn main() {
  let word = "butterfly";
  let length = string.str_len(word);
  io.println(length);  // Prints: 9
}
```

### Making Text LOUD with `string.str_upper()`

Need to make text uppercase? Use `string.str_upper()`. It takes a string and returns the same text in ALL CAPS:

```xiom
fn main() {
  let whisper = "hello";
  let shout = string.str_upper(whisper);
  io.println(shout);  // Prints: HELLO
}
```

There's also `string.str_lower()` which does the opposite — it makes everything lowercase.

### Putting It All Together

Here's a program that uses all three string tricks:

```xiom
fn main() {
  let name = "sam";

  // Glue strings together
  let message = "Welcome, " + name + "!";
  io.println(message);

  // Count the letters
  let count = string.str_len(name);
  io.println(count);

  // Make it uppercase
  let loud = string.str_upper(name);
  io.println(loud);
}
```

Strings are everywhere in programming. Every chat message, every game dialog, every website headline — they're all strings. You just learned how to shape them!

